From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 12:44:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ucode: ubus: read blob values without assuming their
 alignment

ucode's ubus module read 64-bit integers and doubles of a ubus message
through a uint64_t pointer, although blob attributes are only four-byte
aligned: a misaligned load, undefined behaviour, which traps in a UBSan
build, so that uhttpd's ucode handlers died converting such a reply.

Add a patch to ucode that reads every scalar with libubox's
blobmsg_get_*() accessors. It is meant for ucode upstream.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 package/utils/ucode/Makefile                  |  2 +-
 ...ues-without-assuming-their-alignment.patch | 51 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 52 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 package/utils/ucode/patches/120-ubus-read-blob-values-without-assuming-their-alignment.patch

diff --git a/package/utils/ucode/Makefile b/package/utils/ucode/Makefile
index eb6abd6..d05aaa4 100644
--- a/package/utils/ucode/Makefile
+++ b/package/utils/ucode/Makefile
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@
 include $(TOPDIR)/rules.mk
 
 PKG_NAME:=ucode
-PKG_RELEASE:=1
+PKG_RELEASE:=2
 
 PKG_SOURCE_PROTO:=git
 PKG_SOURCE_URL=https://github.com/jow-/ucode.git
diff --git a/package/utils/ucode/patches/120-ubus-read-blob-values-without-assuming-their-alignment.patch b/package/utils/ucode/patches/120-ubus-read-blob-values-without-assuming-their-alignment.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d424baa
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/utils/ucode/patches/120-ubus-read-blob-values-without-assuming-their-alignment.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] ubus: read blob values without assuming their alignment
+
+blob_to_ucv() read 64-bit integers and doubles through a uint64_t
+pointer, but blob attributes are padded to four bytes, so their data is
+only four-byte aligned: a misaligned load, which is undefined behaviour.
+Built with -fsanitize=undefined -fsanitize-trap=undefined, ucode traps
+converting a ubus reply that holds such a value.
+
+Read every scalar with libubox's blobmsg_get_*() accessors, whose
+blobmsg_get_u64() reads two aligned 32-bit words, as libubox's own
+blobmsg_format_json() does for 64-bit integers.
+
+Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+---
+--- a/lib/ubus.c
++++ b/lib/ubus.c
+@@ -774,28 +774,20 @@
+ 
+ 	switch (blob_id(attr)) {
+ 	case BLOBMSG_TYPE_BOOL:
+-		return ucv_boolean_new(*(uint8_t *)data);
++		return ucv_boolean_new(blobmsg_get_bool(attr));
+ 
+ 	case BLOBMSG_TYPE_INT16:
+-		return ucv_int64_new((int16_t)be16_to_cpu(*(uint16_t *)data));
++		return ucv_int64_new((int16_t)blobmsg_get_u16(attr));
+ 
+ 	case BLOBMSG_TYPE_INT32:
+-		return ucv_int64_new((int32_t)be32_to_cpu(*(uint32_t *)data));
++		return ucv_int64_new((int32_t)blobmsg_get_u32(attr));
+ 
+ 	case BLOBMSG_TYPE_INT64:
+-		return ucv_int64_new((int64_t)be64_to_cpu(*(uint64_t *)data));
++		return ucv_int64_new((int64_t)blobmsg_get_u64(attr));
+ 
+ 	case BLOBMSG_TYPE_DOUBLE:
+-		;
+-		union {
+-			double d;
+-			uint64_t u64;
+-		} v;
+-
+-		v.u64 = be64_to_cpu(*(uint64_t *)data);
++		return ucv_double_new(blobmsg_get_double(attr));
+ 
+-		return ucv_double_new(v.d);
+-
+ 	case BLOBMSG_TYPE_STRING:
+ 		return ucv_string_new_length(data, len - 1);
+ 
